threads.body:
This is now the second eager-initialization site. `AgentStarterImpl.start()` already does the same
thing, just later and only under a security manager:

```java
    AgentInstaller.installBytebuddyAgent(instrumentation, extensionClassLoader);

    // LazyStorage reads system properties. Initialize it here where we have permissions to avoid
    // failing permission checks when it is initialized from user code.
    if (System.getSecurityManager() != null) {
      Context.current();
    }
```

With this change that block is a no-op whenever the agent is enabled. The only path where it still
does anything is the `EarlyInitAgentConfig.get().isEnabled() == false` branch, and there nothing
installs the SDK or any instrumentation, so the shaded context storage is never used at all.

Permissions are unaffected by moving it: `AgentClassLoader.getPermissions()` grants
`AllPermission` when security manager support is enabled, and both call sites run entirely on
agent frames.

Suggest dropping `AgentStarterImpl.java` lines 107-111 plus the then-unused
`import io.opentelemetry.context.Context;` (line 8, it is the only usage) in this PR, so there is
one place that owns this ordering instead of two with different rationales.

