threads.body:
This works only because `TestAgentListener` is class-initialized before `AgentInstaller` calls
`ContextStorage.get()` - `TestAgentExtension.extend()` touches `TestAgentListener.INSTANCE` while
extensions are being loaded, which is a few lines earlier in `installBytebuddyAgent`.

If that ever stops holding, `addWrapper` is ignored with only a `FINE` log, `contextStorageInitialized`
stays `false` forever, and `AgentForTestingTest` fails with a bare `expected: true but was: false`
that is indistinguishable from a real regression. Worth documenting the dependency here:

```suggestion
    // record when context storage is initialized so tests can verify the agent startup ordering
    // note that this class must be initialized before AgentInstaller calls ContextStorage.get(),
    // otherwise addWrapper() is silently ignored and the assertion in AgentForTestingTest fails
    // for the wrong reason
    ContextStorage.addWrapper(
        storage -> {
          contextStorageInitialized.set(true);
          return storage;
        });
```

